            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for former, then the Kannada for theft."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಉದಯ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಉದಯ — udaya — \"a rise; a dawn\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆ ರಾಜ್ಯದ ಉದಯ ಒಂದು ಸಣ್ಣ ಹಳ್ಳಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಆಯಿತು. ā rājyada udaya ondu saṇṇa haḷḷiyalli āyitu. The rise of that kingdom began in a small village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸೂರ್ಯೋದಯ is sunrise. Of a kingdom or a leader, its rise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಉದಯ (udaya) is borrowed from Sanskrit udaya, \"rise, rising of the sun\" (CDIAL 1931)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
